  "reason": "The current best (config_033, 0.713 acc) uses multimodal + multiprofile + scvi_n200 + resnet50 + transformer + weighted. The evidence strongly supports this architecture: scvi_n200 > PCA > scgpt for RNA, multiprofile >> singleprofile, transformer ≥ avgpool, and weighted > concat fusion. The remaining untested lever within this proven architecture is the image encoder. Resnet50 alone was very weak (0.208), but contributed meaningfully in the multimodal setting (+0.06 over RNA-only). Upgrading to imagenet_vit_l (config_039) is a single-variable change that directly tests whether a stronger visual representation can push accuracy further. This is the most logical exploitation step: it isolates the image encoder effect while holding all other design choices at their empirically best values, and it preserves the final experiment for a potential further refinement if this succeeds."
}

